<urn:anqr:application-action-model:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "A denominator beneath capabilities. Capability coverage can be complete while behaviour is missing, because one capability can own several actions and an unowned action is invisible at capability level. Every observable product action resolves to a retained capability or carries an explicit non-product disposition; there is no third state." <urn:anqr:graph:application-actions> .
<urn:anqr:application-action-model:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objectiveEvidence> "Derived from the legacy application: 126 store actions, 185 public API query parameters, 33 payload serialisers, 12 client routes, 4 serverless functions, 1 edge function, an MCP server with two tools, one prompt and one resource, 86 locale resources, and a PWA manifest." <urn:anqr:graph:application-actions> .
<urn:anqr:application-action-model:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Parameter mutation is collapsed into one action per control group, each enumerating the store actions it governs. Modelling 126 near-identical set-a-value actions would have produced a larger denominator and a smaller amount of knowledge." <urn:anqr:graph:application-actions> .
<urn:anqr:application-action-model:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "An action is derived from observable product behaviour, never from a file count. Several of the legacy trees with the most files contribute no action at all, because they are one capability's implementation rather than a distinct thing a user or consumer can do." <urn:anqr:graph:application-actions> .
<urn:anqr:application-action-model:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "This model does not claim the actions are implemented. It claims they are the complete set that must be either implemented or explicitly excluded." <urn:anqr:graph:application-actions> .
